.TH CPKG 1 "November 2026" "cpkg" "CatOS Archive Utility Manual"
.SH NAME
cpkg \- pack and unpack .cpkg archives for CatOS and catpm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpkg
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cpkg
is an archive packing and unpacking utility written in Rust by
Denys Laptev for CatOS and
.BR catpm (1).
It packs directory trees and package payloads into
.I .cpkg
archives, unpacks archives into target roots or package database
directories, and exposes library functions consumed by
.BR catpm (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pack \fI<SOURCE_DIR> <OUTPUT_ARCHIVE>\fR
Packs files and subdirectories from
.I <SOURCE_DIR>
into a
.I .cpkg
archive file at
.IR <OUTPUT_ARCHIVE> .
.TP
.B unpack \fI<ARCHIVE> <DEST_DIR>\fR
Unpacks entries from
.I <ARCHIVE>
into
.IR <DEST_DIR> ,
respecting overwrite, force, dry-run, and checksum options.
.SH PACKAGE HOOKS (commands.json)
A package payload directory may include a
.I commands.json
file defining shell commands executed during lifecycle events in
.BR catpm (1):
.PP
.nf
{
  "after_install": ["echo installed test1"],
  "after_reinstall": ["echo reinstalled test1"],
  "after_remove": ["echo removed test1"]
}
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite existing files or directories without prompting.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry-run
Simulate packing or unpacking without writing target files.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-checksum
Skip checksum validation when unpacking if supported.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose diagnostic output.
.SH SECURITY
Avoid parent directory traversal components (\fB..\fR) when creating
archive entries or unpacking into target roots. When invoked through
.BR catpm (1),
target containment and hook commands are additionally validated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cpkg pack pkg-test1/ test1-1.0.0.cpkg
cpkg pack repo-src/ repo.cpkg
cpkg unpack test1-1.0.0.cpkg /tmp/catpm-root
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR catpm (1),
.BR catpm\-config (5),
.BR catpm\-repository (5)
